                <pb facs="0139" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 810.51/378.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Missions in Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Chile,
                            Colombia, Ecuador, Panama, Paraguay, Peru, Uruguay
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 6, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of Treasury says: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In order to arrange program for April meeting of International High
                            Commission, United States Section earnestly solicits from each of the
                            other sections early suggestions of questions and measures requiring
                            immediate consideration and especially a full and free statement of any
                            changes in United States laws, regulations and practices that would
                            facilitate closer financial and commercial relations.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
